request.description:
Liveness probe. Returns `{"status": "ok"}` unconditionally as long as the FastAPI process is running — does NOT verify Gmail OAuth, Phoenix DB reachability, or the roofix-db connection. Used by the compose healthcheck (`ai/roofix/docker-compose.roofix.yml`). Auth: none (internal). See `ROOFIX.md § Endpoints`.

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`) — the process is up; Gmail, Phoenix and roofix-db are not checked:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["status"],
  "properties": {
    "status": {"const": "ok"}
  }
}
```

Snapshot of the bridge's in-memory tick counters. Returns `{started_at, last_tick_at, last_tick_ok, last_tick_error, tick_count, decisions_total, decisions_by_action, decisions_by_source, escalations_total, phoenix_write_failures, dry_run, agent_phase, tick_interval_seconds}`. `dry_run` reflects the effective env var (`DRY_RUN`, default `true`) — check this before running `/tick` to confirm you're not about to write to Phoenix. `escalations_total` counts decisions with `needs_human` or action `escalate`; `phoenix_write_failures` counts decisions whose Phoenix write (update_chatter, a mapped update_milestone, create_project's ensure_entity_and_project) returned ok=false, once per event — a DRY_RUN write succeeds and a milestone event with no mapping writes nothing, so neither is counted, while a mapped milestone whose block name does not resolve is. Counters are process-local: they reset on container restart. Auth: none (internal). See `ROOFIX.md § Endpoints`.

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`) — the in-memory tick counters (they reset on a restart):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "started_at",
    "last_tick_at",
    "last_tick_ok",
    "last_tick_error",
    "tick_count",
    "decisions_total",
    "decisions_by_action",
    "decisions_by_source",
    "escalations_total",
    "phoenix_write_failures",
    "dry_run",
    "agent_phase",
    "tick_interval_seconds"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "started_at": {"type": "string", "format": "date-time"},
    "last_tick_at": {"type": ["string", "null"], "format": "date-time"},
    "last_tick_ok": {"type": ["boolean", "null"]},
    "last_tick_error": {
      "type": ["string", "null"],
      "description": "repr() of the exception the last tick raised"
    },
    "tick_count": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0},
    "decisions_total": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0},
    "decisions_by_action": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}
    },
    "decisions_by_source": {
      "type": "object",
      "propertyNames": {"enum": ["rule", "ai"]},
      "additionalProperties": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}
    },
    "escalations_total": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0,
      "description": "Decisions with needs_human or action escalate"
    },
    "phoenix_write_failures": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0,
      "description": "Decisions whose Phoenix write returned ok=false, once per event: a DB error, PHOENIX_AGENT_USER_ID unset, a mapped milestone block name that does not resolve to one process block, an ambiguous entity / project match on create_project. A DRY_RUN write succeeds, and a milestone event with no mapping writes nothing: neither is counted"
    },
    "dry_run": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "The effective DRY_RUN (default true): check it before /tick"
    },
    "agent_phase": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "AGENT_PHASE as set: `0` chatter + milestones only; `1` adds create / notify"
    },
    "tick_interval_seconds": {"type": "integer"}
  }
}
```

Manually trigger one processing batch immediately, out-of-band with the APScheduler cadence. With an empty body `{}` (or no body), the bridge fetches unread Roofix mail from Gmail via `LISTENER_QUERY` and runs the full pipeline: parse → resolve project → brain decides → optionally write Phoenix (skipped under `DRY_RUN=true`) → mark Gmail read/labeled. Optionally accepts `{"raw_emails": [...]}` (Contract A shape) to feed crafted samples in without touching Gmail — useful for offline testing.

Serialized with the scheduled tick via `_tick_lock` (asyncio.Lock) plus APScheduler's `max_instances=1` — a manual /tick that arrives mid-schedule waits for the in-flight batch to finish, never overlaps. Returns `{records, count}` on success or `{error, records: [], count: 0}` on pipeline failure (still 200). Auth: none (internal). See `ROOFIX.md § Endpoints` and `ROOFIX.md § How it works`.

#### Schemas

Serialized with the scheduled tick (never overlaps). Optional body: none or `{}` fetches unread Roofix mail from Gmail (LISTENER_QUERY); `raw_emails` processes those instead, without touching Gmail. A `raw_emails` that is not a list is FastAPI's 422.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
